  "interpretation": {
    "finding": "Within the first 32.5 s after trace selection, EGO's camera-pose subscription had a 1.713745 s gap between successful RMW takes; depth and optimized-odometry take gaps in that window were 0.255020 s and 0.268764 s. The independent camera-pose observer received through source stamp 32.572 s with a maximum receipt gap of 0.264985 s. EGO's pose message_filters callback took at most 2.970 ms; the longest callback of any traced type was the map-reset service at 9.871 ms. This narrows the observed stall to EGO's pose take/readiness path but does not identify the DDS reader or executor as the cause.",
    "navigation_outcome": "The run-local harness passed its gates, sent the 0.30 m/+30 degree goal, recorded position_yaw_tolerance_held success, and later confirmed landed/disarmed. The bridge phase history records operator_disable followed by normalized_cost_exceeded while in LANDING; these are separate observations and no causal link is asserted. ULog records EV position/yaw/velocity fusion, zero GNSS aiding, and zero dropouts.",
    "root_cause": "UNRESOLVED. The trace contains no publisher-side publish events or message-header identity pairing. No pose-topic taken=0 event was mapped, and the successful-take gap alone cannot distinguish publisher/reader delivery from executor readiness/scheduling.",
    "limitations": [
      "The independent observer and trace are aligned by run window, not by a one-to-one header-stamp match.",
      "Only the EGO process was selected after graph initialization; the upstream pose publisher was not traced.",
      "The callback timing data does not measure time spent waiting in DDS or the executor wait set.",
      "This is a single diagnostic SITL run with a run-local EGO overlay; it is not P5 or GOAL acceptance evidence."
    ],
    "next_step": "For #228, trace the upstream camera-pose publisher and EGO together, correlate source header stamps at publisher and message_filters receipt, and retain executor readiness/wait events. Keep the same low-bandwidth harness and safety gates; do not change QoS, thresholds, or control ownership."
  },
